A node removed from a RedBlackTree is reset (docs/w7.md W7b).

remove() left the removed node's left and right links in place, and
only insert() cleared them. Since those links became CheckedPtrs, a node
out of the tree kept its old neighbours checked: RunLoopGeneric's timers
are such nodes, and a timer that had fired and stayed stopped made
freeing its neighbour crash - WebKit2's BackgroundProcessResponsivenessTimer
as a closed page's web process proxy went (testing.md 18.807). Upstream
has the same code; its other run loops do not keep timers in this tree.

--- a/Source/WTF/wtf/RedBlackTree.h	2026-11-14 14:50:00.566905671 -0300
+++ b/Source/WTF/wtf/RedBlackTree.h	2026-11-14 14:50:00.582195142 -0300
@@ -286,6 +286,11 @@
         } else if (y->color() == Black)
             removeFixup(x, xParent);
 
+        // Z is out of the tree: its links go, as insert() clears a node's
+        // before it goes in. They are CheckedPtrs, and a removed node that
+        // kept them - a timer that fired and stays stopped - held its old
+        // neighbours checked, so freeing one of them crashed.
+        z->reset();
         return z;
     }
     
